+# asynchronous barrier before it reopens graph and block I/O admission
+# on the main AioContext.  A quiescent RCU barrier acknowledges proof
+# bit 4.  A quiescent asynchronous barrier acknowledges AIO proof bit
+# 3.  A complete immutable-root binding retained by the block barrier
+# acknowledges proof bit 5.  Version 10 retains a fully drained
+# incomplete transaction so the host can stage branch-private
+# resources under the same quiescent source-ring barrier.  Version 11
+# binds those stages to the exact template generation.  Version 12
+# additionally binds an explicit empty-local-state parent-resume and
+# child-reinitialize worker plan to the exact plugin-barrier
+# generation.  Version 13 acknowledges plugin-ring proof bit 6 only
+# while the complete retained resource pair remains bound to that
+# active quiescent transaction.  Version 14 additionally binds the
+# registered child-runtime plan into an unconsumed QEMU-owned one-shot
+# adapter and reports its exact adjacent process generations without
+# acknowledging child-reinitialization proof bit 8.  Version 15 also
+# binds that plan and the retained endpoint sources into the exact
+# nondestructive plugin descriptor-replacement, retained-descriptor,
+# and writable-shared-mapping tables.  Version 16 requires a fresh
+# authenticated branch-private diagnostics stream and composes its
+# source-to-stderr replacement into the same sealed child resource
+# plan.  Version 17 additionally retains one authenticated
+# branch-private QMP stream in that plan without closing or
